codex
The run reached hierarchy initialization but the sandbox rejects the Unix socket used by PyTorch’s two DataLoader workers. This is local execution plumbing, not a training failure; the failed hash directory is preserved. Because PLAN-1 permits only the smoke config and forbids algorithm changes, I won’t edit the hierarchy. I’ll use the same unified entry point with a local runtime wrapper that only forces DataLoader workers to zero, and I’ll add an attempt identifier to the smoke config so the overwrite guard retains the failed attempt and reserves a fresh hash.
