index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..abc84bb8495351bc63e1807f0805757d09f5ae03
--- /dev/null
+++ b/configs/smoke/plan1_cifar100_ehsfp_gate.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# PLAN-1 only: bounded CIFAR-100 instrumentation smoke gate.
+# The execution harness deterministically caps the locally cached CIFAR-100
+# partition to 32 train samples/client and 128 validation/test samples.
+# This config is not suitable for accuracy or paper-number comparisons.
+base: ../classification/h-sfp/cifar_our_resnet50_5_10.yaml
+
+is_gpu: false
+iid: true
+num_users: 8
+mid_server: [2]
+epochs: 2
+frac: 1.0
+t1: 1
+t2: 2
+eval_every: 2
+
+local_bs: 16
+ssl_epochs_client: 1
+ssl_epochs_edge: 1
+syn_epochs_cloud: 1
+syn_samples_per_class: 16
+use_lr_schedule: false
+
+smoke_train_samples_per_client: 32
+smoke_eval_samples: 128
+
+# Keep the smoke paths small while ensuring the full preset can exercise them.
+memory_size: 10000
+memory_top_k: 2
+prc_num_samples: 2
+
+# full_e_hsfp enables the simulator; eliminate simulated timeouts so the
+# instrumentation gate observes every selected client in both rounds.
+cold_start_probability: 0.0
+function_timeout_probability: 0.0
+
+# Distinguishes the sandbox-safe zero-worker retry from the preserved failed
+# preflight directory; it has no training semantics.
+smoke_attempt_id: plan1_cpu_tiny_v2
diff --git a/docs/optimization_loop/DECISIONS.md b/docs/optimization_loop/DECISIONS.md
index 0eeb6dc5ff8ff16a4dbeb4a0c60ef7e4a28852db..baef727d925ecf35866bd0c5792b093aaae9264a
--- a/docs/optimization_loop/DECISIONS.md
+++ b/docs/optimization_loop/DECISIONS.md
@@ -13,3 +13,9 @@
 ## Phase-0 disposition
 
 No mandated core component remains a demonstrated dead path after the plumbing repairs: memory, reliability, PRC, dropout, distinct config hashes, checkpoint mismatch rejection, and result isolation all pass deterministic tests. Optional residual-generator and dropout-consistency flags remain unintegrated and must not be claimed as verified. Phase 1 may be planned, but it should begin with one bounded smoke run that inspects runtime counters before any grid.
+
+## PLAN-1 decision
+
+1. Do not promote to Phase 1. The bounded `baseline_hsfp` CPU smoke crashed at `classification/H-SFP/hierarchy.py:781`: CPU autocast emitted `bfloat16` client prototypes, but the edge convolution bias remained FP32 (`RuntimeError: Input type (c10::BFloat16) and bias type (float) should be the same`). The `full_e_hsfp` preset completed because reliability-weighted aggregation promoted its inputs to FP32, so the two-preset gate is asymmetric and criterion (a) is not met.
+2. Stop after the declared two presets. No grid or hyperparameter tuning is authorized; a targeted Phase-0 plan must make the baseline CPU dtype path consistent before PLAN-1 is rerun.
+3. Treat exact reliability variance and scalar PRC loss as unresolved instrumentation gaps. The persisted counters prove 461 nonuniform reliability-weight calls and 564 nonzero PRC calls, but the requested min/max/variance and scalar PRC values are not written to JSONL.
